sd document view accessibles: take the SolarMutex before the disposed check.

AccessibleDocumentViewBase::getAccessibleChild/getAccessibleAtPoint/getBackground and the
getAccessibleChildCount/getAccessibleChild overrides of AccessibleDrawDocumentView and
AccessibleOutlineView called ensureAlive() and then took only the object's own mutex (or none).
Called from the gtk3 accessibility bridge, which runs without the SolarMutex, they could pass the
check while another thread holding the SolarMutex disposed the view and its children manager.
They now take the SolarMutex first. The overrides must lock too: otherwise a call holding the
object's mutex would wait for the SolarMutex in the base class while dispose(), under the
SolarMutex, waits for the object's mutex. Upstream bug (same code in LibreOffice 26.8.1.1 and
26.8.3.1).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_sd_a11y (hst-sd-docview-a11y-dispose-race-test.patch).
